Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:38:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 5347: a named target is reached at the 4th and 5th degree
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

find_warm_path stopped at 3 hops and the members' own chains at three
people in the middle, so a 5th-degree target was unreachable. The graph
walk now goes to 5 hops in two steps: up to 3 as before, and only when
nothing is that close, on to 5. A long walk that runs out of time keeps
the near answer rather than reading as an outage. Member chains add four
in the middle (owner's member -> member -> member -> member holding the
target); a chain that comes back through one of its own people is dropped.

The max_hops line reads "Optional, 1–5 (default 5)." in the chat tool and
the connector (Misho's yes to the exact text, 16 Oct).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
